  "diagnosis": {
    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_AS_READ",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 0.54,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.12,
    "rationale": "The undiluted readings plateau at about 0.53 from 5 h onward. I diluted the 18 h aliquot to check whether that plateau was a reader ceiling. The dilution-corrected values (reading × dilution) were 0.536 at 3×, 0.575 at 10× (2 replicates), 0.468 at 20× and 0.62 at 30× (2 replicates). All of these are close to the undiluted 0.531. They do not rise steadily with dilution, which a saturating reader would produce. The spread looks like noise, which is larger at the very low raw readings of 0.02. The plateau therefore looks like genuine stationary phase, and biomass is at the level the undiluted readings indicate."
  },
